{"parentUuid":"560d79b0-f3a5-4ada-aebb-85dedaa6c261","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/ledgerline","sessionId":"buried-07","version":"2.0.14","gitBranch":"report/q3-active","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_0114fLmBhkeFj6a5ABDAbgOo","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the cause. When two CRM accounts are merged, the CRM keeps the absorbed account as its own row, sets merged_into to the surviving account's crm_id, and leaves its status as it was: 1,847 merged rows still say active. Both rows carry the same ledger_customer_id, so both match the paid invoices and the customer is counted twice. 412 of them have a paid invoice in Q3, which is exactly the difference to 13,500. So finance's dashboard must already leave out rows with merged_into set.\n\nThe fix is to drop rows with merged_into before counting: the surviving row is the customer. Is that how the CRM is meant to work, or is it a bug on their side?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":633,"output_tokens":543}},"uuid":"099f4d27-2ff0-435a-beec-a5c6fe306053","timestamp":"2026-10-07T08:51:08.000Z","requestId":"req_011C9BXpJAQyK4Fd91te71Sy"}
{"parentUuid":"099f4d27-2ff0-435a-beec-a5c6fe306053","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/ledgerline","sessionId":"buried-07","version":"2.0.14","gitBranch":"report/q3-active","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"It's how it works. The CRM never deactivates merged accounts, it only fills merged_into, and the dashboard filters them out. Exclude them."},"uuid":"52a0522b-3b10-488a-852f-9494ae99d4b4","timestamp":"2026-10-07T08:52:08.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"52a0522b-3b10-488a-852f-9494ae99d4b4","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/ledgerline","sessionId":"buried-07","version":"2.0.14","gitBranch":"report/q3-active","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01b6Z7fIcdwVMYxgEvi8WvFh","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WsWt7hdoLelg0SpptJtdSL","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/home/dev/ledgerline/scripts/reports/q3_active.py","old_string":"def active(df: pd.DataFrame, paid: set[str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    return df[(df[\"status\"] == \"active\") & df[\"ledger_customer_id\"].isin(paid)]","new_string":"def active(df: pd.DataFrame, paid: set[str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    # The CRM keeps a merged account as its own row with merged_into set and its status unchanged, often\n    # 'active', and with the survivor's ledger_customer_id. Counting it counts the customer twice.\n    survivors = df[df[\"merged_into\"] == \"\"]\n    return survivors[(survivors[\"status\"] == \"active\") & survivors[\"ledger_customer_id\"].isin(paid)]"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":454,"output_tokens":144}},"uuid":"96685a89-83ff-4da0-85f3-39024997ba4e","timestamp":"2026-10-07T08:52:12.000Z","requestId":"req_011CvCwF6HngmGC4XaIsy5Uz"}
